WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.735
President Biden's personal attorney, Bob

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:03.169
Bauer, released a statement

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:05.705
in just the last a little over an hour

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:07.474
saying that the Justice Department

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:09.476
conducted a search of the Wilmington,

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:10.610
Delaware, home

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.879
and found additional materials

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:14.514
with classified markings.

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:15.615
Now, Bauer

00:00:15.615 --> 00:00:17.384
stresses that this search

00:00:17.384 --> 00:00:18.852
was done in coordination

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:20.520
with the president's personal attorneys.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:21.988
Both the personal attorneys

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:22.989
and lawyers

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:23.523
from the White House

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:25.625
counsel's office were on hand

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:26.793
for that search.

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:27.861
A source has also told us

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:28.862
that it was specifically

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:30.697
conducted by the FBI.

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:32.198
And what Bauer said

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:33.967
is that they opened up the home

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:35.535
for this search

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:37.037
that included a search of the living,

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:39.272
the working and the storage areas.

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:40.740
And Wilmington, Delaware.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:41.341
And I want to read

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:42.308
you a bit of his statement

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:44.177
that gets into exactly

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:45.912
what types of materials

00:00:45.912 --> 00:00:46.913
they were looking through.

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:48.782
Bauer wrote in a statement, quote,

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:50.283
DOJ had full access

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:50.917
to the president's

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:52.952
home, including personally handwritten

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:56.256
notes, filed papers, binders, memorabilia

00:00:56.256 --> 00:00:57.824
to do lists, schedules

00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:59.893
and reminders going back decades.

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:01.728
DOJ took possession of materials

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:02.962
it deemed within the scope

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:03.997
of its inquiry,

00:01:03.997 --> 00:01:05.331
including six items

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:06.299
consisting of document

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:07.767
with classification markings

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.602
and surrounding materials.

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:11.237
Some of which were from the president's

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:12.272
service in the Senate

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.507
and some of which were from his tenure

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:15.809
as vice president.

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:17.644
DOJ also took for further

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:19.712
review personally handwritten notes

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.748
from the vice presidential years.

00:01:21.748 --> 00:01:22.515
Now, the White House

00:01:22.515 --> 00:01:23.283
special counsel,

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.184
Richard Saber,

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:24.851
said that neither

00:01:24.851 --> 00:01:26.453
President Biden nor First Lady

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:28.054
Jill Biden were on hand

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:29.489
for this search yesterday,

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:31.891
which took close to 13 hours.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:32.759
But really,

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:33.693
this marks

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:36.296
the fifth instance that we know of

00:01:36.296 --> 00:01:37.230
where documents

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.832
were found to either

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:41.034
locations tied to President Biden.

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:41.734
There was first

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:42.502
that discovery

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:43.837
on November 2nd

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:44.370
at the Penn

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:45.105
Biden Center,

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:46.606
that private office

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.041
Biden used when he left

00:01:48.041 --> 00:01:49.809
the Obama administration.

00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:50.877
There was another search

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:52.579
conducted in Wilmington, Delaware,

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:53.713
on December 20th

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:56.015
and then also another on January 11th.

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:57.250
And the following day,

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.285
more documents were found but yesterday

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:01.221
did amount to the fifth time

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:03.656
the documents had been found at locations

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:05.058
tied to President Biden.

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:05.592
Of course,

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:07.093
it wasn't until much later

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:07.627
after that

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.829
initial search on November 2nd.

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:11.264
It wasn't until two months later

00:02:11.264 --> 00:02:12.031
that it was revealed

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:14.167
that those documents had even been found

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:16.102
publicly to this press.

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:17.203
But this all comes

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:17.804
as the White House

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:20.740
has been grappling with this ongoing saga

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:22.742
related to the classified documents.

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:23.309
And one thing

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:23.910
that they've faced

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.411
some criticism over

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:27.780
is their initial unwillingness

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.115
to disclose

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:30.650
the finding of these documents

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:31.050
right away.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:31.918
And I want to

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:33.052
have you listen to

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:34.020
what President Biden

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:35.755
had to say earlier this week

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:36.489
when he was asked

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:38.224
whether he had any regrets

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:40.026
about their decisions not to

00:02:40.026 --> 00:02:41.327
disclose things right away.

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:47.000
That revealed

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:49.769
back in December before the big time this

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:51.604
law

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:54.407
as we found out,

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:55.375
we found a handful

00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:57.177
of documents were failed,

00:02:57.177 --> 00:02:59.112
were filed in the wrong place.

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:00.346
We're fully cooperating.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:00.880
Looking forward

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.715
to getting this resolved quickly.

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:04.450
I think you're going to find there's

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:04.984
nothing there.

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:06.152
I have no regrets.

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:06.853
I'm following

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:08.621
what the lawyers have told me.

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:09.956
They want me to do

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:11.658
exactly what we're doing.

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:14.460
There's no they're there.

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:16.930
Of course,

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.097
this is a remarkable

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:19.232
string of events

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:20.366
that has unfolded over

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:21.901
the course of the past two weeks.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.636
And now with the FBI

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:25.471
searching the home of a current

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:27.473
sitting president, of course,

00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:28.741
the White House

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:29.509
has been quick

00:03:29.509 --> 00:03:30.109
to point out

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:31.411
that they are trying to cooperate

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:33.580
fully every step of the way

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.748
with the special counsel's investigation,

00:03:35.748 --> 00:03:37.083
with the Justice Department,

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:38.585
with the National Archives.

00:03:38.585 --> 00:03:39.018
Of course,

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:40.920
they're trying to draw this contrast

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:41.821
with the way that former

00:03:41.821 --> 00:03:43.223
President Donald Trump

00:03:43.223 --> 00:03:45.158
handled the classified documents

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:45.692
down in Mar

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:47.327
a Lago as he is being investigated

00:03:47.327 --> 00:03:49.095
down there for obstruction.

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:50.563
But the White House trying to make clear

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:52.932
that they are trying to follow each step

00:03:52.932 --> 00:03:53.933
that the Justice Department

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:54.968
has laid out for them

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:56.636
and cooperate in this matter.

00:03:56.636 --> 00:03:58.204
But at this moment,

00:03:58.204 --> 00:04:01.674
just yesterday, more documents were found

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:02.442
at that

00:04:02.442 --> 00:04:03.243
Wilmington, Delaware,

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:05.345
home, bringing the total

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:06.746
known classified documents

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:07.914
found between the home

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:09.749
and then also that private office

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:10.917
to close to 30.

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:11.784
I will also note

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:12.518
that President Biden

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:14.621
