00:06:28.755 --> 00:06:31.457
executed, they did find

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:32.925
several classified documents.

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:34.026
I think it was around 100,

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:36.629
if my memory serves me at Mar a Lago.

00:06:36.863 --> 00:06:38.998
But that aside, in this case,

00:06:38.998 --> 00:06:40.900
you have a sitting president's

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:43.603
personal residence being searched

00:06:43.903 --> 00:06:47.240
by the FBI for nearly 13 hours.

00:06:47.407 --> 00:06:49.442
This is truly extraordinary.

00:06:49.442 --> 00:06:50.476
It's historic.

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:51.077
And in terms

00:06:51.077 --> 00:06:52.645
of the national security implications,

00:06:52.645 --> 00:06:53.312
you say, Marc,

00:06:53.312 --> 00:06:55.481
you don't believe that this

00:06:55.481 --> 00:06:56.582
this is going to have

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:58.151
serious implications on that front.

00:06:58.151 --> 00:06:59.285
But armed the war.

00:06:59.285 --> 00:07:01.220
What would prosecutors be looking at?

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:01.621
They're going to

00:07:01.621 --> 00:07:02.922
take these classified documents.

00:07:02.922 --> 00:07:04.690
They're going to look at everything

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:05.825
that they've gathered

00:07:05.825 --> 00:07:07.794
through the course of this investigation.

00:07:07.794 --> 00:07:09.128
Walk us through the process

00:07:09.128 --> 00:07:10.196
of what they're looking for

00:07:10.196 --> 00:07:11.831
to see if laws had been broken here.

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:15.601
Pamela, thank you so

00:07:15.601 --> 00:07:17.670
much for having me on.

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:20.406
So at the base,

00:07:20.406 --> 00:07:21.240
this is

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:23.075
deeply embarrassing to the president

00:07:23.075 --> 00:07:26.245
and I think a big distinguishing factor

