00:08:35.281 --> 00:08:36.115
And we don't know if those were

00:08:36.115 --> 00:08:37.049
classified materials

00:08:37.049 --> 00:08:39.886
or not from Biden's time as service.

00:08:40.186 --> 00:08:41.821
What would additional materials

00:08:41.821 --> 00:08:43.756
be on those with classified markings?

00:08:43.756 --> 00:08:46.125
How would they help investigators

00:08:46.125 --> 00:08:47.393
in this investigation?

00:08:47.393 --> 00:08:50.263
Why would they be pertinent here?

00:08:51.297 --> 00:08:53.733
So the FBI and the special counsel

00:08:53.733 --> 00:08:55.034
are investigating

00:08:55.034 --> 00:08:57.403
what is a mishandling of documents

00:08:57.403 --> 00:08:58.437
case now.

00:08:58.437 --> 00:09:00.606
And that question is

00:09:00.606 --> 00:09:02.041
were these documents mishandled?

00:09:02.041 --> 00:09:03.509
The answer is yes.

00:09:03.509 --> 00:09:05.511
Why were they mishandled?

00:09:05.511 --> 00:09:07.613
Was that intentional or unintentional

00:09:07.647 --> 00:09:09.148
that's being inquired of?

00:09:09.148 --> 00:09:10.683
Were they

00:09:10.950 --> 00:09:12.518
disseminated to anybody

00:09:12.518 --> 00:09:13.786
while they were mishandled?

00:09:13.786 --> 00:09:15.321
That's another question that they ask.

00:09:15.321 --> 00:09:16.355
So they have to answer these

00:09:16.355 --> 00:09:17.256
particular questions

00:09:17.256 --> 00:09:18.157
to make a determination

00:09:18.157 --> 00:09:19.091
whether or not

00:09:19.091 --> 00:09:21.394
is mishandling of classified documents

00:09:22.895 --> 00:09:26.365
rises to the level of a criminal charge

00:09:26.365 --> 00:09:27.733
or whether it's inadvertent

00:09:27.733 --> 00:09:29.535
and therefore not criminal

00:09:29.535 --> 00:09:30.570
in terms of

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:32.371
what's in the documents themselves.

00:09:32.371 --> 00:09:33.306
That remains to be seen.

00:09:33.306 --> 00:09:35.207
But I remember him

00:09:35.207 --> 00:09:37.143
when I did the indictment,

00:09:37.143 --> 00:09:38.844
my independent counsel investigation,

00:09:38.844 --> 00:09:39.879
and we interviewed

00:09:39.879 --> 00:09:41.280
former President George Herbert

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:43.382
Walker Bush in his offices in Houston.

00:09:43.382 --> 00:09:44.550
We said to him, Mr.

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:44.850
President,

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:46.385
do you have any recollection of this?

00:09:46.385 --> 00:09:48.955
He said, well, let me go check my diary.

00:09:49.121 --> 00:09:50.156
And he went out, came

00:09:50.156 --> 00:09:51.824
back, came back with his diary.

00:09:51.824 --> 00:09:52.325
He said, No,

00:09:52.325 --> 00:09:54.226
I have no indication of that,

00:09:54.226 --> 00:09:55.628
but I do have an indication of this.

00:09:55.628 --> 00:09:57.396
So here's a present for president

00:09:57.396 --> 00:09:59.498
with a diary in his personal office.

00:09:59.632 --> 00:10:02.602
Which probably had classification issues

00:10:02.768 --> 00:10:03.469
that surround them.

00:10:03.469 --> 00:10:04.804
So I don't think

00:10:04.804 --> 00:10:06.839
that is in and of itself significant,

00:10:07.139 --> 00:10:07.940
but it is

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:10.977
what the prosecutors need to ascertain

00:10:10.977 --> 00:10:12.378
before they can make a determination

00:10:12.378 --> 00:10:13.412
about whether something

00:10:13.412 --> 00:10:14.580
is classified or not.

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:16.616
To what Mark said, though,

00:10:16.616 --> 00:10:17.917
and I think needs

00:10:17.917 --> 00:10:21.754
reiterating is these document cases

00:10:22.188 --> 00:10:23.122
point to the fact

00:10:23.122 --> 00:10:25.391
that there is overclassification

00:10:25.625 --> 00:10:27.293
in the United States government

00:10:27.293 --> 00:10:28.995
and that there are so many documents

00:10:28.995 --> 00:10:31.097
that shouldn't be classified,

00:10:31.097 --> 00:10:32.264
that are classified.

00:10:32.264 --> 00:10:33.332
That gets politicians

00:10:33.332 --> 00:10:35.067
who are unintentional

00:10:35.067 --> 00:10:35.935
in their handling

00:10:35.935 --> 00:10:36.602
these documents,

00:10:36.602 --> 00:10:39.605
but sloppy in these sort of legal jams.

00:10:39.605 --> 00:10:40.906
And I think that one of the things

00:10:40.906 --> 00:10:42.942
that Congress should be doing is looking

00:10:42.942 --> 00:10:44.276
at the classification system.

